#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Rebuild the public class website in /workspace/school/site/  (v2: everything relevant to teaching).

Collects, from /workspace/school/: slide decks, daily lesson plans + sub plans (plans/*.pdf), worksheets/printables/cards,
teacher keys, games, curriculum docs, calendars, portfolio kits, cooking, newsletters, family handouts, the SEL check-in how-to,
and a few markdown docs rendered to PDF into /workspace/school/site-build/.
There is NO content scan (Grant, 2026-10-27: nothing we make has real identifiable student information). Only path exclusions apply. Nothing is uploaded by this script;
templates/publish_site.sh pushes the result. Run:  python3 update_site.py [--zip]
Rules (Grant, 2026-10-27): publish all teaching material, teacher keys go in "Teacher resources" sections, student 2-letter codes are fine.
Skipped by path only: staff handbook, gemini notes, internal files (INTERNAL_SKIP), team-ideas/, data/ (except the SEL check-in how-to),
ahead/ (build-ahead drafts), cards-build/, superseded versions (-v1), cover option files, exact duplicate files.
Inclusion courses (gen ed classes with modified Level 2 materials for SLE students): one folder per course in
/workspace/school/inclusion/<slug>/ with a course.json -> site page inclusion/<slug>.html. A course is built only when
course.json has "publish": true, or when run with --preview-inclusion (review copy; the daily routine never passes it).
See /workspace/school/templates/README-site.md and README-inclusion.md.
"""
